                <pb facs="0175" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <head>58. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>During a TASS broadcast at 7 p.m. EDT on August 30, 1961, the Soviet Union
                    announced that it was resuming atomic testing. For text, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Documents on Disarmament, 1961</hi>, pages 347-348.
                    Through intelligence channels, the U.S. Government had prior knowledge of the
                    announcement and began drafting a statement that was released by the White House
                    at approximately 9 p.m. (Memoranda of telephone conversations: Rusk-Stevenson,
                    Rusk-Bohlen, Rusk-Bundy, and Rusk-Wiesner, all the evening of August 30;
                    Department of State, Rusk Files: Lot 72 D 192, Telephone Conversations) For text
                    of the announcement, <hi rendition="#italic">see Documents on Disarmament,
                        1961</hi>, pages 348-350. The memorandum of Rusk’s telephone conversation
                    with Wiesner indicates that Dean’s recall, announced in the statement, was
                    initiated by the President.</p>
            </div>
